### 2026-08-27 (1st) - Tempo-arc mapping MERGED; the gate can finally read a real mix
**Brain:** Claude (spec, measurement, oracle, judgment, 5 of 7 commits) + Codex (TempoMap build, 4 review rounds) + MiniMax (fail-closed review). Suite 450 -> **472 passed / 6 skipped / 0 failed** on merged main.

**The headline:** the render gate hard-refused every real mix, because it converted beats to seconds with one scalar. It now carries a piecewise `TempoMap`. Merge of `feat/render-gate-tempo-map` (7 commits).

**The model was settled by measurement, not assumption.** Live interpolates tempo linearly over the BEAT axis, so beat->time is a log integral `dt = (60/m)*ln(v1/v0)`. Against Sam's real 84-minute V16 bounce: flat-Manual predicts the arrangement end at 5200.876 s, the log integral at 5031.098 s, and the audio actually stops at 5031.302 s. **A 169.6 s error reduced to 0.204 s.** Verified by an independently written oracle - separate parser, separate integral, itself checked against a closed form and a 2M-step Riemann sum - over 42,128 probes including exactly on and just past every tempo knee, plus monotonicity, inverse round-trip and exact flat reproduction: zero measurable error. Codex's figures matched Claude's to the decimal from two separately written code paths.

**Gotcha for anyone touching this:** the envelope carries a `-63072000` sentinel ("value before the timeline"). Integrate across it and you get 31,174,703 seconds.

**Honest limits SHIPPED rather than hidden.** A ~19.5 ppm residual remains (96 ms over the mix; fitted across all 16 solo runs, R^2 0.969, residual RMS 5.3 ms). Mechanism UNKNOWN - buffer quantisation (0.37 ms), the linear-in-time alternative (2 ms) and float precision are ruled out by calculation, and the V16 ALS predates that render by five days so we cannot prove they correspond. **No scale correction was applied**; fitting one to an unpaired render would be calibrating to noise. Consequently, on a tempo arc `grid_fold` reports and does NOT gate, and `boundary_click` skips every boundary BY NAME (its +/-2 ms window cannot be trusted when the fit scatter alone is wider). New `check_map_vs_render` catches the realistic gross case - the wrong tempo model applied whole-mix - by comparing endpoints with no fitted constant, and its compensated-interior blind spot is PINNED by a test asserting the wrong map passes.

**Every review round found something real, and three of the findings were Claude's own.** MiniMax (narrow, on the fail-closed set) returned DON'T SHIP: 2 of 3 cases were genuine silent-lossy paths and were fixed, 1 was judged correct on the evidence and documented + pinned instead of changed. Codex then reviewed the commits it did NOT write and returned DON'T SHIP four times before SHIP/PROVEN. Its findings, all closed: an unbounded arc downgrade that made an arbitrarily wrong map non-blocking; `is_flat` too coarse to decide boundary clicks; an incomplete unidentified-envelope scan (blank `PointeeId`, and it only ran with zero matches); **a fitted MEAN used as a safety bound** - 19.5 ppm has 5.3 ms scatter and is not a proven maximum, and as an allowance it grew until it swallowed the very 101.9 ms a known-wrong map produces; an oversold endpoint check; an uncapped FAIL tolerance that would pass a six-minute error on a ten-hour mix; plus a test of Claude's that hid its assertions behind a conditional, and a report that listed a SKIPPED check as "clean".

**The V10 pin caught a regression no review did:** the per-boundary filter applied the residual to FLAT maps too, skipping every boundary past ~51 s of the 54-minute control the gate was calibrated on. Pins earn their keep - and they only do so when they actually run, which needed `DJ_MIX_TEST_PROJECT` pointed read-only at the real corpus (both the V10 decimal pin and the V16 truth pin had been silently SKIPPING in the build sandbox).

**First real check results on V16, and they matter:** three `loop_verbatim` FAILs at 5:26, 12:40 and 76:39 (min r = 0.84 / 0.81 / 0.67). Ruled out as a tempo artefact - all six report loops sit inside ramps, tempo moves only ~0.09 BPM across each (sub-millisecond per iteration), and three of the six PASS under identical conditions. These look like genuine defects of the class Sam heard in V10 ("loops cut in the wrong place") and need his ears. Also raised, unverified: 3 transition dips (2.6-3.8 dB) and 2 exposed-solo warnings.

**Also found:** `_grid_fold_median` can lock onto an OFFBEAT lattice - two of 16 probes returned quarter- and half-beat aliases, and with them in a clean R^2 of 0.969 collapses to 0.365, so a real drift signal reads as noise. Carded.

