# Automated DJ Mixes

## What This Is

Automated DJ mix pipeline for Wired Masters showreels. Takes a folder of pre-tagged dance tracks and produces a sequenced, warped, gain-leveled Ableton Live 12 session (ALS file) from a known-good template. Sam drops tracks in, says "mix these," and gets a ready-to-review session back â€” harmonic sequencing, beat-matched, transitions automated, levels balanced. He loads it in Ableton, listens through, tweaks, and it's done.

Born from the realisation that the grunt work of DJ mixing (key analysis, Camelot sequencing, warping, gain leveling, crossfades, filter automation) is entirely rule-based and takes hours that could be automated.

## Tech Stack

- **Python 3.x** â€” main orchestrator and all pipeline modules
- **Librosa** â€” transient/downbeat detection, energy analysis (fallback when Rekordbox unavailable)
- **pyloudnorm** â€” LUFS measurement for gain staging
- **mutagen** â€” reading key/BPM from ID3/Vorbis tags (written by Mixed In Key)
- **pyrekordbox** â€” reading Rekordbox ANLZ files (beat grids, phrase analysis)
- **Ableton Live 12** â€” target DAW, ALS file format (gzip-compressed XML)
- **Mixed In Key** â€” key + BPM analysis (run separately, writes to file tags)
- **Rekordbox 7** â€” legacy/debug-only parser and desktop path; not used by canonical `/mix`

Not in V1: Max for Live (future enhancement for real-time automation), pyproject.toml packaging.

## Architecture

```
Source/automated_dj_mixes/
â”œâ”€â”€ __init__.py
â”œâ”€â”€ orchestrator.py        â€” Main pipeline controller, --visualize mode
â”œâ”€â”€ analysis.py            â€” Tag reading, transient detection, LUFS
â”œâ”€â”€ sequencer.py           â€” Camelot wheel logic, harmonic path
â”œâ”€â”€ warping.py             â€” Per-beat warp markers from the selected certified grid
â”œâ”€â”€ automation.py          â€” AutomationPoint + gain offset calc
â”œâ”€â”€ als_generator.py       â€” Template-based ALS XML patching (multi-clip per track)
â”œâ”€â”€ mix_plan.py            â€” Immutable N-track production intent + per-track playback policy
â”œâ”€â”€ rekordbox_reader.py    â€” Rekordbox ANLZ parser (PSSI phrases, PQTZ beat grid)
â”œâ”€â”€ rekordbox_waveform.py  â€” PWV5/PWV4 colour waveform parser (4th analysis signal)
â”œâ”€â”€ features.py            â€” Per-beat features (RMS + bass + PWV5) with disk cache
â”œâ”€â”€ phrase_viz.py          â€” Factual Interval records + viz colour collapse
â”œâ”€â”€ cue_candidates.py      â€” Ranked CueCandidate API (5 cue types + confidence + visual_hint + amplitude + MIK paths)
â”œâ”€â”€ mik_reader.py          â€” Mixed In Key 11 GEOB tag + SQLite reader (cues, beat grid, energy)
â”œâ”€â”€ amplitude_analysis.py  â€” 1s RMS envelope analysis (first_drop, first_break, outro_start, clean-loop-window detector)
â”œâ”€â”€ report.py              â€” Per-track CSV + per-mix Markdown reports
â”œâ”€â”€ waveform_preview.py    â€” Blank-canvas preview PNG (for writing visual hints before pipeline run)
â”œâ”€â”€ desktop_analyzer.py    â€” MIK metadata UI for `/mix`; legacy Rekordbox automation remains isolated
â””â”€â”€ config.py              â€” Settings loader
```

Canonical pipeline: optional MIK metadata â†’ owned stem grid â†’ Demucs sections + Kick Detector V3 â†’ sequencing â†’ warping â†’ arrangement â†’ automation â†’ ALS/reconciliation/visual validation. Rekordbox is not launched or read.

ALS generation is **template-based** â€” a real Ableton Live 12 session is decompressed, studied, and used as the base. The script patches in tracks, clips, warp markers, automation lanes, and gain offsets. Never builds XML from scratch.

### Template: `DJ Mix Template 2026.als`

- **Track 1**: "Session Time" â€” HOFA Project Time only, no audio. Always skip.
- **Tracks 2-12**: "2-Audio" through "12-Audio" â€” each has identical effects chain:
  - `StereoGain` (Utility) â€” stereo/mono, width, gain, balance, bass mono @ 120Hz
  - `ChannelEq` â€” 3-band EQ (Low/Mid/High) + output gain. **Use Low band for bass kills** (cleaner than filter)
  - `AutoFilter2` Id="1" â€” **Low-pass**, SVF, 24dB slope, freq at 20kHz (fully open). Sweep DOWN to cut highs.
  - `AutoFilter2` Id="3" â€” **High-pass**, SVF, 24dB slope, freq at 20Hz (fully open). Sweep UP to cut lows.
- **Device hierarchy**: `AudioTrack > DeviceChain > Devices > AudioEffectGroupDevice > Branches > AudioEffectBranch > DeviceChain > AudioToAudioDeviceChain > Devices`
- Each parameter has a unique `AutomationTarget Id` â€” must be found dynamically per track

### Key automation targets (per track)

| Parameter | XML Element | Purpose |
|-----------|------------|---------|
| Mixer Volume | `Mixer > Volume > AutomationTarget` | Crossfade curves |
| Utility Gain | `StereoGain > Gain > AutomationTarget` | LUFS-based gain offsets |
| LP Filter Freq | `AutoFilter2[0] > Filter_Frequency` (Type=0) | Low-pass sweep â€” cut highs |
| HP Filter Freq | `AutoFilter2[1] > Filter_Frequency` (Type=1) | High-pass sweep â€” cut lows |
| Channel EQ Low | `ChannelEq > Low > Gain > AutomationTarget` | Bass kill (cleaner than filter) |

## How to Run

```powershell
pip install -r requirements.txt
$env:PYTHONPATH="Source"
python -m automated_dj_mixes.orchestrator --input "Tracks/" --output "Output/"
```

Later: `pyproject.toml` + editable install (`pip install -e .`).

